# PROVENANCE: measured from a genuine DESFire EV3 2K with Proxmark3 on 2026-11-01 (the second
# genuine EV3 2K used for the other hardware_physical_ev3_2k_* captures; random UID).
# PROVISIONAL BATCH "iso-write-2026-11-01": every vector of this batch carries
# `capture-batch: iso-write-2026-11-01` and `capture-status: provisional`. If the card
# turns out to be faulty these captures can be thrown away together: the append-only gate
# allows deleting a provisional capture (and nothing else about it). To find them all:
#   grep -l 'capture-batch: iso-write-2026-11-01' tests/vectors/desfire/v*/*/*.vec
# and see docs/capture-batches.md.
#
# What this measures: how an open (staged, not yet committed) native transaction interacts
# with ISO 7816 commands on the same application. Card file 3 is a free linear record file
# (ISO id 1003, four 4-byte records); each section first empties it (ClearRecordFile +
# CommitTransaction) so sections replay independently. Observed on the card:
#   * A staged native WriteRecord survives other successful commands (native commands,
#     ISO SELECT, a successful ISO READ RECORD) and CommitTransaction publishes it.
#   * Any FAILING command (a native error, an ISO READ RECORD answering 6985) discards the
#     staged write: CommitTransaction then answers 0C (nothing to commit).
#   * A successful ISO APPEND RECORD writes its record at once and does NOT publish the
#     staged native write; the staged write is discarded (Abort and Commit both answer 0C).
# The ATS line (E080 => ...) is copied from the sibling captures of this card: this
# Proxmark3 session performs RATS itself, so the card's ATS answer was not on the wire log.
name: genuine EV3 2K ISO commands versus a staged native transaction (provisional batch)
case-id: hardware-physical-ev3-2k-iso-write-transaction
origin: physical-card
capture-batch: iso-write-2026-11-01
capture-status: provisional
feature-version: 6
source: physical-card-proxmark3
requires: record-files
uid: 04112233445566
picc-generation: EV3
picc-storage: 2048
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-key-len: 16
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-hardware-version: 04010133001605
picc-software-version: 04010103001605

# Equivalent freely provisioned replay fixture: application 123456 with ISO file ids and
# linear record file 3 (ISO id 1003, four 4-byte records, free access).
scan
status 905A00000300000000 => 00
status 90CA0000071234560F2100E100 => 00
status 905A00000312345600 => 00
status 90C100000C03031000EEEE04000004000000 => 00

# control: AbortTransaction discards a staged native WriteRecord
field-off
scan
frame-exchange E080 => 0565810280
frame-exchange 02905A00000312345600 => 029100
frame-exchange 0390EB0000010300 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290C7000000 => 029100
frame-exchange 03903B00000B03000000040000AABBCCDD00 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290A7000000 => 029100
frame-exchange 0390F50000010300 => 030300EEEE0400000400000000009100
frame-exchange 0290BB0000070300000000000000 => 0291BE

# ISO APPEND RECORD after a staged native WriteRecord, then AbortTransaction
field-off
scan
frame-exchange E080 => 0565810280
frame-exchange 02905A00000312345600 => 029100
frame-exchange 0390EB0000010300 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290C7000000 => 029100
frame-exchange 0300A4000C021003 => 039000
frame-exchange 02903B00000B03000000040000AABBCCDD00 => 029100
frame-exchange 0300E200000411223344 => 039000
frame-exchange 0290A7000000 => 02910C
frame-exchange 0390F50000010300 => 030300EEEE0400000400000100009100
frame-exchange 0290BB0000070300000000000000 => 02112233449100

# ISO APPEND RECORD after a staged native WriteRecord, then CommitTransaction
field-off
scan
frame-exchange E080 => 0565810280
frame-exchange 02905A00000312345600 => 029100
frame-exchange 0390EB0000010300 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290C7000000 => 029100
frame-exchange 0300A4000C021003 => 039000
frame-exchange 02903B00000B03000000040000AABBCCDD00 => 029100
frame-exchange 0300E200000411223344 => 039000
frame-exchange 0290C7000000 => 02910C
frame-exchange 0390F50000010300 => 030300EEEE0400000400000100009100
frame-exchange 0290BB0000070300000000000000 => 02112233449100

# control: a staged native WriteRecord survives another successful native command
field-off
scan
frame-exchange E080 => 0565810280
frame-exchange 02905A00000312345600 => 029100
frame-exchange 0390EB0000010300 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290C7000000 => 029100
frame-exchange 03903B00000B03000000040000AABBCCDD00 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290F50000010300 => 020300EEEE0400000400000000009100
frame-exchange 0390C7000000 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290BB0000070300000000000000 => 02AABBCCDD9100

# control: a staged native WriteRecord survives an ISO SELECT
field-off
scan
frame-exchange E080 => 0565810280
frame-exchange 02905A00000312345600 => 029100
frame-exchange 0390EB0000010300 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290C7000000 => 029100
frame-exchange 03903B00000B03000000040000AABBCCDD00 => 039100
frame-exchange 0200A4000C021003 => 029000
frame-exchange 0390C7000000 => 039100
frame-exchange 0290BB0000070300000000000000 => 02AABBCCDD9100

